{'symbol': 'EQIX', 'date': '2019-10-15 22:30:00', 'title': 'PENSANDO SYSTEMS ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS RECEIVED $145 MILLION IN FUNDING FROM HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE COMPANY, LIGHTSPEED VENTURE PARTNERS, EQUINIX, INC. (REIT), AND OTHER INVESTORS.', 'text': 'PENSANDO SYSTEMS ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS RECEIVED $145 MILLION IN A ROUND OF FUNDING CO-LED BY NEW INVESTORS, HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE COMPANY (NYSE:HPE) AND LIGHTSPEED VENTURE PARTNERS ON OCTOBER 16, 2019. THE TRANSACTION ALSO INCLUDED PARTICIPATION FROM NEW INVESTOR, EQUINIX, INC. (REIT) (NASDAQGS:EQIX) AND AND OTHERS. THE COMPANY HAS RAISED $278 MILLION IN FUNDING TILL DATE. AS A PART OF THE TRANSACTION, MARK POTTER, CHIEF TECHNOLOGY OFFICER OF HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE AND BARRY EGGERS, A PARTNER OF LIGHTSPEED VENTURE PARTNERS JOINED THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF THE COMPANY.'}{'symbol': 'EQIX', 'date': '2019-10-13 22:30:00', 'title': 'EQUINIX APPOINTS MICHAEL MONTOYA AS CHIEF INFORMATION SECURITY OFFICER', 'text': "EQUINIX, INC. ANNOUNCED THE APPOINTMENT OF MICHAEL MONTOYA AS CHIEF INFORMATION SECURITY OFFICER (CISO), FURTHER BOLSTERING THE COMPANY'S COMMITMENT TO SECURITY. IN THIS ROLE, MONTOYA IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LEADING EQUINIX'S GLOBAL CYBERSECURITY RISK PROGRAM. HIS RESPONSIBILITIES WILL INCLUDE EVOLVING THE COMPANY'S INFORMATION SECURITY PROGRAM AND DEFINING THE COMPANY'S FUTURE CYBERSECURITY ROADMAP, ENTERPRISE RISK MANAGEMENT AND COMPLIANCE PROGRAMS. MONTOYA WILL WORK CLOSELY WITH EQUINIX'S PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT, OPERATIONS, IT, COMPLIANCE AND BUSINESS CONTINUITY TEAMS TO HELP ENSURE THE COMPANY HAS A WORLD-CLASS APPROACH TO SECURING ITS GLOBAL ASSETS AS WELL AS PROVIDING THE MOST SECURE ENVIRONMENT FOR CUSTOMERS."}{'symbol': 'EQIX', 'date': '2019-10-15 22:30:00', 'title': 'PENSANDO SYSTEMS ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS RECEIVED $145 MILLION IN FUNDING FROM HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE COMPANY, LIGHTSPEED VENTURE PARTNERS, EQUINIX, INC. (REIT), AND OTHER INVESTORS.', 'text': 'PENSANDO SYSTEMS ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS REC